.\" Manpage for warpzone.
.\" Contact: elifulkerson@gmail.com
.TH WARPZONE 1 "June 2026" "warpzone 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
warpzone \- seamless PTY wrapper with on-demand output capture and local pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B warpzone
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B warpzone
launches an interactive shell (or any other program) inside a pseudo-terminal
(PTY) and acts as a transparent terminal shim in front of it. Under normal
operation you type and see output as usual (this is called
.BR PASSTHRU " mode)."
.PP
At any time \(em except while the child is using the alternate screen buffer \(em
you can press
.B Ctrl-]
to enter a local mini-editor
.RB ( PIPE_ENTRY
mode) and type a shell pipeline, for example
.IR "grep foo | wc -l" .
Pressing
.B Enter
commits the pipeline:
.B warpzone
sends Enter to the child program, captures the child's output for a short
window
.RB ( CAPTURE
mode), and then feeds that captured output into your pipeline, which is executed
.B on the local machine
via
.IR "/bin/sh -c" .
.PP
This is useful for post-processing the output of a program whose environment
lacks your local tools \(em a remote
.BR ssh (1)
session, a serial console, a container, or a restricted appliance shell \(em
using the utilities installed on the local host.
.PP
The captured output is written to an anonymous temporary file under
.IR /tmp ,
created with
.BR mkstemp (3)
and immediately unlinked, so it does not persist after the pipeline finishes.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B PASSTHRU
Normal operation. Keystrokes are forwarded to the child; the child's output is
printed to the screen.
.TP
.B PIPE_ENTRY
Entered with
.BR Ctrl-] .
A green
.RB \(lq | \(rq
marker is shown and keystrokes are buffered locally to build a pipeline. Nothing
is sent to the child until the pipeline is committed.
.TP
.B CAPTURE
Entered when a non-empty pipeline is committed with
.BR Enter .
The child's output is recorded silently while a dim status overlay (byte count,
idle time, capture age, end mode, and a throughput sparkline) is drawn on the
last terminal row.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl-] " (in PASSTHRU)"
Enter PIPE_ENTRY; prints a green
.RB \(lq | \(rq.
.TP
.IR printable " (in PIPE_ENTRY)"
Append the character to the local pipeline.
.TP
.B Backspace " (in PIPE_ENTRY)"
Erase one character; backspacing over the marker cancels PIPE_ENTRY.
.TP
.B Enter " (in PIPE_ENTRY)"
Commit the pipeline: send Enter to the child and begin CAPTURE. Committing an
empty pipeline simply leaves PIPE_ENTRY.
.TP
.BR Ctrl-C ", " Ctrl-] " (in PIPE_ENTRY)"
Cancel PIPE_ENTRY and return to PASSTHRU.
.TP
.B Ctrl-] " (in CAPTURE)"
End capture immediately and run the pipeline.
.SH CAPTURE END CONDITIONS
While capturing, recording stops at the first of:
.TP
.B Quiet gap (default)
No PTY output for
.B --gap-ms
milliseconds (default 200).
.TP
.B Manual end
.B Ctrl-]
is pressed.
.TP
.B Byte guardrail
.B --max-bytes
bytes have been captured (disabled by default).
.TP
.B Time guardrail
.B --max-seconds
have elapsed since capture began (disabled by default).
.PP
Use
.B --manual-end
to disable the quiet-gap heuristic, so capture ends only via
.B Ctrl-]
or a guardrail.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --shell " PATH"
Program to exec inside the PTY. Default:
.IR /bin/bash .
.TP
.BI --shell-arg " ARG"
Add an argument for the PTY child program. May be repeated. If no
.B --shell-arg
is given,
.B warpzone
adds
.B -i
by default for an interactive shell.
.TP
.BI --gap-ms " N"
Quiet-gap in milliseconds to end capture. Default 200;
.B 0
disables gap-ending.
.TP
.B --manual-end
Disable quiet-gap ending. Capture then ends only via
.B Ctrl-]
or a guardrail.
.TP
.BI --max-bytes " N"
End capture after
.I N
bytes have been captured.
.B 0
disables (default).
.TP
.BI --max-seconds " N"
End capture after
.I N
seconds.
.B 0
disables (default).
.TP
.BR --version ", " -V
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit.
.PP
Command-line options override values loaded from the configuration file.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
If present,
.I ~/.warpzonerc
is read at startup, before command-line arguments are parsed; command-line
options therefore take precedence.
.PP
The file is UTF-8 text with one
.IR key = value
setting per line. Whitespace around keys and values is tolerated, blank lines
are ignored, and lines beginning with
.RB \(lq # \(rq
are comments.
.PP
Supported keys:
.TP
.B shell
(string) Path to the PTY child program, e.g.\&
.IR /bin/zsh .
.TP
.B shell_arg
(string) Adds one argument; repeat the line for multiple arguments.
.TP
.B gap_ms
(int \(>= 0) Quiet-gap end condition in milliseconds.
.TP
.B manual_end
(bool)
.IR true / false / yes / no / on / off / 1 / 0 .
.TP
.B max_bytes
(int \(>= 0) Capture size guardrail in bytes.
.TP
.B max_seconds
(int \(>= 0) Capture time guardrail in seconds.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Use zsh and disable gap-ending
shell=/bin/zsh
shell_arg=-i
manual_end=true
max_seconds=10
max_bytes=1048576
.fi
.RE
.SH SIGNALS AND JOB CONTROL
In PASSTHRU mode,
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGQUIT ", " SIGTERM ", " SIGHUP ", " SIGTSTP ", and " SIGCONT
are caught by
.B warpzone
and forwarded to the PTY foreground process group, so
.BR Ctrl-C ", " Ctrl-Z ,
and job control behave as in a normal terminal. Window-size changes
.RB ( SIGWINCH )
are propagated to the child. In PIPE_ENTRY and CAPTURE, these signals are
dropped so they do not surprise the child.
.SH NOTES AND LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
PIPE_ENTRY is disabled while the child is in the alternate screen buffer (e.g.\&
.BR vim (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR top (1)),
because injecting a visible marker into a full-screen app is disruptive. In that
state,
.B Ctrl-]
beeps and prints a notice; exit the full-screen app first.
.IP \(bu 2
During CAPTURE, normal keystrokes are ignored; only
.B Ctrl-]
(to end capture) is honored.
.IP \(bu 2
The status overlay and sparkline use Unicode block glyphs, so a UTF-8-capable
terminal is recommended.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Wrap the default interactive bash:
.B warpzone
.TP
Wrap a remote session and filter its output with local tools:
.B warpzone --shell /usr/bin/ssh --shell-arg user@host
.TP
Use zsh with a longer quiet-gap:
.B warpzone --shell /bin/zsh --gap-ms 500
.TP
Capture a long-running command, ending manually but capped at 30 seconds:
.B warpzone --manual-end --max-seconds 30
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.warpzonerc
Optional configuration file (see CONFIGURATION FILE).
.TP
.I /tmp/warpzoneXXXXXX
Anonymous temporary capture file, unlinked immediately after creation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B warpzone
exits 0 after the child program exits normally, and a non-zero status on a
fatal startup error (for example, failure to allocate a PTY).
.SH SECURITY
The pipeline typed in PIPE_ENTRY is executed locally via
.IR "/bin/sh -c" ,
with the captured child output supplied on its standard input. Captured output
is treated as data on stdin and is not interpreted as a shell command, but the
pipeline itself is your own command line, so the usual care with shell
metacharacters applies.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR script (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR sh (1)
